## Summary

Hardens the structured session-event ledger landed by https://github.com/openclaw/crabfleet/pull/75.

- terminal sessions accept only exact, side-effect-free replays during the five-minute credential window;
- structured event messages and recursive payload values are redacted before D1/R2 persistence, including credential-shaped fields, embedded headers/tokens, URL userinfo, complete or split private-key blocks, and common secret-key forms;
- exact replay of a pre-hardening row atomically sanitizes D1 and durably requeues terminal archive finalization, so transient R2 failures and finalization races retry safely;
- structured events no longer replace legacy message-event summary anchors;
- legacy event rows and public/archive serialization remain backward compatible.

## Root cause

The initial endpoint authenticated stopped sessions for retry but also allowed new terminal inserts. It serialized additive payloads without a persistence-boundary credential scrubber, treated every event type as a legacy summary anchor, and had no replay-compatible repair path for rows written before redaction.

## Proof

- `pnpm run check`
- `pnpm test` — 753 passed
- `pnpm run build`
- `pnpm exec wrangler deploy --dry-run`
- `pnpm audit --audit-level=high` — no known vulnerabilities
- fresh Wrangler-local D1 migration chain through migration 0032
- populated legacy migration preserved `null / message / null` compatibility fields
- real local Worker + Wrangler D1/R2 proof:
  - authenticated active append returned `duplicate: false`;
  - semantic replay returned `duplicate: true`;
  - terminal legacy replay returned a sanitized duplicate;
  - new terminal history returned 403 and a wrong token returned 401;
  - D1 stored only redacted message/payload values and set terminal finalization pending;
  - R2 published a sanitized replacement archive and removed the obsolete credential-bearing object.
  - a fresh, complete, same-count active-session archive was forcibly replaced immediately, bypassing normal cadence, and its obsolete R2 object was removed.
- final autoreview: clean, no actionable findings
- Public Model Identifier Gate: PASS; the candidate, tests, generated/build surfaces, and this proof contain no model identifiers.

No release, version bump, tag, registry publication, deployment, or dependency change is included.
